On Sun, Apr 19, 2015 at 3:52 PM, Alex Burka <durka42@gmail.com> wrote:

> I don't have a strong feeling on which "quick fix" is better. The issue
> that makes it messy is it's hard to do uniformly, because each has its own
> wrinkle: CGV=>CVGV creates tosmabru if the CGV was initial, whereas
> CGV=>CV'V sometimes creates slinku'i or lujvo-shaped words, the latter of
> which is a tcizbaga-type situation (and I know some BPFK members don't
> think that's a problem).
>

The apostrophe fix is more "lojbanic". in the sense that it uses forms that
already exist in lujvo instead of forms exclusive to fu'ivla/cmevla, so the
resulting words look more like core lojban words. But, as you say, it
doesn't always work.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

